          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Generally, an
            %em enhanced gauge symmetry
            refers to the appearance of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            with a larger
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            than may be superficially apparent.
          %h3#on_coincident_dbranes On coincident D-branes
          %p
            A famous case is the enhanced gauge symmetry in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+fields"} Chan-Paton gauge fields
            of coincident
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundle"} complex line bundle
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundle"} principal U(1)-bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            of them coincide the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            is expected to enhance from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U(1))^n
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
            (or the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+unitary+group"} special unitary group
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(n)
          %p
            Mathematically this gauge enhancement on D-branes is modeled by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Baum-Douglas+geometric+cycle"} Baum-Douglas geometric cycle
            model for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-homology"} K-homology
            (
            %a{:href => "#ReisSzabo05"}> Reis-Szabo 05, def. 1.5 and p. 16
            ,
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#Szabo08"} Szabo 08, p. 4
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \overset{\phi}{\hookrightarrow} X
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            equipped with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec+structure"} spin^c structure
            and with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundle"} complex vector bundle
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi W
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (W,\phi,E_1)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi W
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (W,\phi,E_2)
            with the same underlying manifold (“coincident D-brane
            = succeed "\u201D)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            is identified with the single cycle carrying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi W
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi W
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∼
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi W
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (W,\phi, E_1) + (W, \phi, E_2)
                  \\;\sim\;
                  (W, \phi, E_1 \oplus E_2)
                  \\,.
          %p
            If here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_i
            has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank"} rank
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_i
            and hence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+group"} structure group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n_i)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1 \oplus E_2
            has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+group"} structure group
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+group"} product group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n_1) \times U(n_2)
          %p
            In particular the sum of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            coincident cycles each carrying a line bundle yields a rank-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            vector bundle with structure group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U(1))^n
            = succeed "-vector" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            D-branes coincide.
          %h3#from_massless_bps_states From massless BPS states
          %p
            In the context of the realization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theories"} super Yang-Mills theories
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theories"} effective field theories
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring+theory"} superstring theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+branes"} BPS branes
            in the string background becomes BPS states of the SYM theory. These become massless as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cycles"} cycles
            on which the BPS charge is supported shrink away (at boundary points of the given
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
          %p
            Examples include
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
            fibers and on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} G₂-manifolds
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+singularities"} ADE singularities
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibrations"} elliptic fibrations
            making
            = succeed "-fibrations" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            on singular elliptic fibrations. See at
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+lift+of+gauge+enhancement+on+D6-branes"} M-theory lift of gauge enhancement on D6-branes
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} M-theory on G₂-manifolds
                the section
                = succeed ";" do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "M-theory+on+G2-manifolds#EnhancedGaugeGroups"} Nonabelian gauge groups and chiral fermions at orbifold singularities
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
                the section
                %em
                  %a{:href => "F-theory#Fbranescan"} F-brane scan
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+F-theory+and+heterotic+string+theory"} duality between F-theory and heterotic string theory
                \.
          %h3#for_mk6_branes_at_adesingularities For MK6 branes at ADE-singularities
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/blow-up"} blow-up
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-singularity"} ADE-singularity
            is given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+spheres"} Riemann spheres
            that touch each other such as to form the shape of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dynkin+diagram"} Dynkin diagram
            whose A-D-E label corresponds to that of the given
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+subgroup+of+SU%282%29"} finite subgroup of SU(2)
          %p
            This statement is originally due to (
            %a{:href => "#duVal1934I"}> duVal 1934 I, p. 1-3 (453-455)
            ). A description in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyper-K%C3%A4hler+geometry"} hyper-Kähler geometry
            is due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Kronheimer89a"} Kronheimer 89a
          %p
            Quick survey of this fact is in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Reid87"} Reid 87
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Slodowy80"} Slodowy 80
          %p#InStringTheory
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            this fact is interpreted in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+enhancement"} gauge enhancement
            of the
            = succeed "-lift" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MK6"} MK6
            at an ADE-singularity (
            %a{:href => "enhanced+gauge+symmetry#Sen97"}> Sen 97
            ):
          %p
            %img{:alt => "ADE 2Cycle", :src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/ADESingularity.jpg", :width => "760"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Equivariant+homotopy+and+super+M-branes"} HSS18
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+lift+of+gauge+enhancement+on+D6-branes"} M-theory lift of gauge enhancement on D6-branes
            for more.
          %h3#on_m9branes On M9-Branes
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Horava-Witten+theory"} Horava-Witten theory
            there is supposed to be gauge enhancement over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M9-branes"} M9-branes
            such as to identify their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            theory with
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E8"} E8
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
          %p
            Under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
            the M9-brane may be identified with the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/O8-plane"} O8-plane
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/O8DualToM9.jpg", :width => "600"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              from
              %a{:href => "#GKSTY02"} GKSTY 02, section 3
          %p
            This may be used to understand the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+enhancement"} gauge enhancement
            to
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E8"} E8
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+groups"} gauge groups
            at the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic
            boundary of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Horava-Witten+theory"} Horava-Witten theory
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/ViaO8GaugeEnhancementOnM9.jpg", :width => "600"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              from
              %a{:href => "#GKSTY02"} GKSTY 02, section 3
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spontaneously+broken+symmetry"} spontaneously broken symmetry
          %h2#references References
          %h3#ReferencesOnCoincidentDBranes On coincident D-branes
          %p
            The idea that on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            coincident D-branes there is gauge enhancement to
            = succeed "-gauge" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(N)
          %ul
            %li#Witten95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              , section 3 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Bound States Of Strings And
                  = succeed "-Branes" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %strong 460
              (1996) 335-350 [
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(95)00610-9"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(95)00610-9
              ,
              = succeed "]" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9510135"} arXiv:hep-th/9510135
          %p
            There, this is an “obvious guess” (first line on
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9510135#page=8"} p. 8
          %p Subsequently, most authors cite this obvious guess as a fact; for instance the review:
          %ul
            %li#Myers03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Myers"}> Robert Myers
              , section 3 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Nonabelian Phenomena on D-branes
              %strong 20
              (2003) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0303072"}> arXiv:hep-th/0303072
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/0264-9381/20/12/302"} doi:10.1088/0264-9381/20/12/302
          %p
            Discussion in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+conformal+field+theory"} boundary conformal field theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#FuchsKasteLercheLutkenSchweigert00
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrgen+Fuchs"}> Jürgen Fuchs
              , P. Kaste,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+Lerche"} Wolfgang Lerche
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Schweigert"} Christoph Schweigert
              = succeed "," do
                %em Boundary Fixed Points, Enhanced Gauge Symmetry and Singular Bundles on K3
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0007145"} arXiv:hep-th/0007145
          %p
            By actual computation in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string+field+theory"} open string field theory
            “convincing evidence” for the nonabelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            on coincident D-branes was found, numerically, in (see bottom of p. 22)
          %ul
            %li#ColettiSigalovTaylor03
              Erasmo Coletti, Ilya Sigalov,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Washington+Taylor"} Washington Taylor
              = succeed "," do
                %em Abelian and nonabelian vector field effective actions from string field theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0306041"} arXiv:hep-th/0306041
          %p Similar numerical derivation, as well as exact derivation at zero momentum, is in
          %ul
            %li#BerkovitsSchnabl03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Berkovits"}> Nathan Berkovits
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schnabl"} Martin Schnabl
              = succeed "," do
                %em Yang-Mills Action from Open Superstring Field Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0307019"} arXiv:hep-th/0307019
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1126-6708/2003/09/022"} doi:10.1088/1126-6708/2003/09/022
          %p The first full derivation seems to be claimed by:
          %ul
            %li#Lee16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taejin+Lee"}> Taejin Lee
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Covariant open bosonic string field theory on multiple D-branes in the proper-time gauge
              %strong 71
              12 (2017) 886–903 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.01473"}> arXiv:1609.01473
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.3938/jkps.71.886"} doi:10.3938/jkps.71.886
          %p surveyed in
          %ul
            %li#Lee17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taejin+Lee"}> Taejin Lee
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Deformation of the Cubic Open String Field Theory
              %strong 768
              (2017) 248 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.06154"}> arXiv:1701.06154
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physletb.2017.02.065"} doi:10.1016/j.physletb.2017.02.065
          %p
            That on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-branes"} D0-branes
            this reproduces the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} BFSS matrix model
            and on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%28-1%29-branes"} D(-1)-branes
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/IKKT+matrix+model"} IKKT matrix model
            is shown in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taejin+Lee"}> Taejin Lee
              ,
              %em
                Covariant Open String Field Theory on Multiple D
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                \-Branes
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.06402"}> arXiv:1703.06402
              )
          %p
            Discussion of gauge enhancement on coincident D-branes in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Baum-Douglas+geometric+cycles"} Baum-Douglas geometric cycles
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-homology"} K-homology
            is in
          %ul
            %li#ReisSzabo05
              Rui Reis,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Szabo"} Richard Szabo
              %em Geometric K-Homology of Flat D-Branes
              ,Commun.Math.Phys. 266 (2006) 71-122, Journal of the Korean Physical Society December 2017, Volume 71, Issue 12, pp 886–903 (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0507043"}> arXiv:hep-th/0507043
              )
          %p reviewed in
          %ul
            %li#Szabo08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Szabo"}> Richard Szabo
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em D-branes and bivariant K-theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0809.3029"} arXiv:0809.3029
          %p
            Derivation via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+parameterized+stable+homotopy+theory"} rational parameterized stable homotopy theory
            applied to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} The brane bouquet
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vincent+Braunack-Mayer"}> Vincent Braunack-Mayer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Gauge+enhancement+of+Super+M-Branes"} Gauge enhancement of Super M-Branes
              %strong 371
              (2019) 197-265 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.01115"}> arXiv:1806.01115
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-019-03441-4"} doi:10.1007/s00220-019-03441-4
          %h3#on_mbranes_at_adesingularities On M-branes at ADE-singularities
          %p
            The picture of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+lift+of+gauge+enhancement+on+D6-branes"} M-theory lift of gauge enhancement on D6-branes
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Sen97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
              , Section 2,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Note on Enhanced Gauge Symmetries in M- and String Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9707123"} arXiv:hep-th/9707123
          %p Review of the standard lore of gauge enhancement in M-theory includes
          %ul
            %li#Barrett06
              Adam B. Barrett, section 2.3 (following
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#AcharyaGukov04"} Acharya-Gukov 04
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  M-Theory on Manifolds with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
                  Holonomy
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0612096"} arXiv:hep-th/0612096
          %p (…)
          %h3#general General
          %p Original articles include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                , section 4.6 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+Theory+Dynamics+In+Various+Dimensions"} String Theory Dynamics In Various Dimensions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9503124"} arXiv:hep-th/9503124
            %li#HullTownsend95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Hull"}> Chris Hull
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Enhanced Gauge Symmetries in Superstring Theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9505073"} arXiv:hep-th/9505073
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Aspinwall"}> Paul Aspinwall
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Enhanced Gauge Symmetries and K3 Surfaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9507012"} arXiv:hep-th/9507012
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Hull"}> Chris Hull
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Duality, Enhanced Symmetry and Massless Black Holes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://physics.usc.edu/Strings95/Proceedings/pdf/hull.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                M. Bershadsky,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ken+Intriligator"} Ken Intriligator
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shamit+Kachru"} Shamit Kachru
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Morrison"} David Morrison
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometric Singularities and Enhanced Gauge Symmetries
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9605200"} arXiv:hep-th/9605200
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Candelas"}> Philip Candelas
                , Eugene Perevalov, Govindan Rajesh,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Toric Geometry and Enhanced Gauge Symmetry of F-Theory/Heterotic Vacua
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9704097"} arXiv:hep-th/9704097
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mirjam+Cvetic"}> Mirjam Cvetic
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Hull"} Chris Hull
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Wrapped Branes and Supersymmetry
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9709033"} arXiv:hep-th/9709033
            %li#AcharyaGukov04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bobby+Acharya"}> Bobby Acharya
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergei+Gukov"} Sergei Gukov
                = succeed "," do
                  %em M theory and Singularities of Exceptional Holonomy Manifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0409191"} arXiv:hep-th/0409191
            %li#HalvorsonMorrison15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Halverson"}> James Halverson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Morrison"} David Morrison
                %em
                  On Gauge Enhancement and Singular Limits in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 2
